      {
        "id": 114639,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-14T21:55:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Ah, you see, I have multiple environment token bags. I probably don't need to do that, but we'll see how it goes. One with lava, one with monorail, one with dinos.</p><p>If it's for a scenario, it might need to go in that scenario bag. Haven't quite got my head round how to organise that yet.</p><p>I'm a big fan of bagging things so I can just pull out the exact bags I need for a particular situation. Each character has everything they need except the panel in one bag - I figure I'll spread out the panels so people can pick who they want to play, and then grab the bags for those characters. If we're playing a scenario I'll pull the appropriate scenario bag.</p><p>I know, I'm pretty anal about it. But I can't stand having to paw through mixed bags to stuff to find that one thing I want.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:46:36.184Z",
